From a36d7de44a644154857a3534e85e78fbbd5df8ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:48:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/26] B70-QSA-Q01: off-by-default qualification hooks for the
 QSA side caches

New common/qsa_debug.py, every flag read once at import; with none set the
serving path only tests a module constant.

- B70_QSA_DEBUG_RING=raise|warn: QSAMetadataBuilder.build (ring group) keeps
  a host mirror of each ring block's last written position and checks that a
  step starting inside a compression group finds that group's committed keys
  in the ring (catches an unaligned prefix/offload hit, a ring too narrow for
  the speculative lookahead, a ring block shared by two live requests).
  Skipped under graph capture; costs three small device->host copies.
- B70_QSA_DEBUG_DUMP=<dir> (+ _LAYERS): after steps with prefill rows, rank 0
  saves each prefill request's compressed-key rows in logical order and the
  selected blocks of its last row, so cold / prefix-hit / CPU-reload paths of
  the same prompt can be compared (tools/b70_qsa/qsa_engine_lifecycle.py).
- B70_QSA_DEBUG_TIES=1: counts top-k rows whose boundary is an exact tie.
- B70_QSA_GRAPH_CHECK=1: at C1 target-graph capture only, the QSA side-cache
  rows the step writes are compared after the eager pass and after replay,
  and the null block before/after; a mismatch disables that graph key.
